To solve this, let's find the pattern of powers of 3 modulo 8.

\begin{align*}
3^1 &\equiv 3 \pmod{8} \\
3^2 &\equiv 9 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \\
3^3 &\equiv 3 \cdot 3^2 \equiv 3 \cdot 1 \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \\
