\end{align*}

We observe that $3^2 \equiv 1 \pmod{8}$, and the powers of 3 repeat every two steps. To simplify $3^{1234}$, notice that $1234 = 2 \times 617$, an even number. Therefore, we can write:

\begin{align*}
3^{1234} &\equiv (3^2)^{617} \equiv 1^{617} \equiv 1 \pmod{8}
\end{align*}

Thus, the remainder when $3^{1234}$ is divided by 8 is $\boxed{1}$.

